aria-live=3D"off" aria-busy=3D"false" dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-dura=
tion: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node=3D"0"=
>This is a classic "Spatial Join" and "Reverse Search" problem. Given you a=
re using <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"83">Java 25</b>, =
<b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"92">Hibernate 7.2</b>, and=
 <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"111">JTS</b>, you have ac=
cess to modern Jakarta Persistence features and advanced spatial functions.=
</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">Since you need to filter by parent propertie=
s and perform a distance-based calculation for every result, a <b data-path=
-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"107">Specification</b> or a <b data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"126">Criteria Query</b> is the most =
flexible approach, while the "Danger Zone" calculation is best handled via =
a specialized <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"242">Subquer=
y</b> or a <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"256">Lateral Jo=
in</b>.</p><hr data-path-to-node=3D"2"><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"3">1. The S=
trategy: "The Lateral Approach"</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"4">To efficient=
ly find the <i data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"24">closest</i=
> <code data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"32">DangerZone</code>=
 for every <code data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"53">Destinat=
ion</code>, a standard SQL join would create a Cartesian product. Instead, =
we want to find the single closest record within 500 meters.</p><h3 data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"5">2. Implementation: The Specification</h3><p data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"6">I recommend using the <b data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-no=
de=3D"22">Criteria API</b>. This allows you to join up the hierarchy (<code=
 data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"78">Destination</code> -&gt;=
 <code data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"93">Location</code> -&=
gt; <code data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"105">ParentVersion<=
/code> -&gt; <code data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"122">Paren=
