ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node=3D"0">Yes, shi=
fting the calculation to the database is the most efficient way to handle t=
his. For spatial data, doing the "Heavy Lifting" in the DB (PostGIS/Spatial=
 DB) allows you to leverage <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"186">GisT (Generalized Search Tree) indexes</b>, which make "within 500=
m" queries nearly instantaneous.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">Since you ar=
e using <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"20">Hibernate 7.2<=
/b> and <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"38">Java 25</b>, y=
ou can use <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"59">Virtual Col=
umns</b> (via <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"80">@Form=
ula</code>) or a <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"95">Nativ=
e View</b>. Given your requirement to switch between <code data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"149">draft</code> and <code data-path-to-node=
=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"159">published</code> versions, a <b data-path=
-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"181">Mapping Projection</b> or a <b da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"205">Lateral Join</b> is the cl=
eanest architectural choice.</p><hr data-path-to-node=3D"2"><h3 data-path-t=
o-node=3D"3">1. The Strategy: The Lateral Join (Most Efficient)</h3><p data=
-path-to-node=3D"4">Instead of calculating on the fly in Java, we tell the =
Database: <i data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"65">"For every D=
estination found, go find its single closest DangerZone within 500m and ret=
urn its stats as part of the row."</i></p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"5">2. Im=
plementation: The Repository Method</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"6">You can =
use a <b data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"14">Native Query</b>=
 in your Spring Data Repository. This handles the version switching (<code =
data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"95">isDraft</code>) and the s=
patial math in one trip to the database.</p><response-element class=3D"" ng=
