=3D"9">3. Key Spatial Functions Used</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"10">By per=
forming these in the <code data-path-to-node=3D"10" data-index-in-node=3D"2=
7">SELECT</code> clause, the database engine optimizes the math:</p><ul dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"11"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"11,0,0"><b data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"11,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0"><code data-path-to-node=3D"11,0,0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"0">ST_DWithin</code></b>: Uses the spatial index to q=
uickly discard any DangerZone further than 500m.</p></li><li><p data-path-t=
o-node=3D"11,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">=
<code data-path-to-node=3D"11,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">::geography</co=
de></b>: Casts your geometry to geography so that <code data-path-to-node=
=3D"11,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"54">500</code> is treated as <b data-path=
-to-node=3D"11,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"72">meters</b> rather than degree=
s.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"11,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,2=
,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0"><code data-path-to-node=3D"11,2,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">ST_Azimuth</code></b>: Returns the north-based clockwise angl=
e (bearing) between the destination and the zone center.</p></li><li><p dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"11,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,3,0" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"0"><code data-path-to-node=3D"11,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">&lt;-&g=
t;</code> Operator</b>: This is a "Nearest Neighbor" operator that uses the=
 spatial index to sort by distance extremely fast.</p></li></ul><hr data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"12"><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"13">4. Handling the Result in Ja=
va 25</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"14">Since the query returns extra columns=
